{"title":"Heterogeneous Element-Aware Cross-Version Differencing of Scientific Documents via Layout-Aware Alignment and Structure-Aware Reasoning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14117","arxiv_id":"2607.14117","authors":["Zhen Yin","Wenkang An","Hao Wang","Keran You"],"year":2026,"abstract":"Proposes a layout-aware cross-version differencing framework that decomposes scientific PDFs into typed text, table, formula, and figure elements, aligns corresponding elements using spatial, content, and structural compatibility, and localizes semantic changes between document revisions."}
{"title":"Time Present and Time Past: Benchmarking Large Language Models on Temporally Evolving Document Understanding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.08512","arxiv_id":"2608.08512","authors":["Mahbub E Sobhani","Md. Faiyaz Abdullah Sayeedi","Fahmid Hasan Chowdhury","Md Adnan Arefeen","Farig Sadeque","Md. Faizul Bari","Swakkhar Shatabda"],"year":2026,"abstract":"Introduces TIDE, a benchmark for question answering over evolving official documents where the correct answer depends on which document version was valid at the queried time. It explicitly tests version resolution and rejection of temporally invalid versions."}
{"title":"VersionRAG: Version-Aware Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Evolving Documents","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.08109","arxiv_id":"2510.08109","authors":["Daniel Huwiler","Kurt Stockinger","Jonathan Fürst"],"year":2025,"abstract":"Presents a version-aware RAG framework that models document evolution with a hierarchical graph containing version sequences, content boundaries, and changes between document states. Retrieval routes version-sensitive questions through version filtering and change-tracking paths."}
{"title":"SentryLine: Evidence-Grounded Question Answering over Evolving Documents in Oncology Care","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08364","arxiv_id":"2609.08364","authors":["Tampu Ravi Kumar","Gaurav Najpande","Muhammad Ali Khan","Kaneez Zahra Rubab Khakwani","Karan Kathuria","Shorya Azriel Moses","Yuvraj Kalia","M Bassam Sonbol","Irbaz Bin Riaz","Vivek Gupta"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-09-08","abstract":"Describes evidence-grounded QA over living oncology guidelines. The system returns inline citations, temporal verification, and drift information when guideline documents have changed across versions."}
{"title":"M3Grounder: Mask-Based Multi-Span and Multi-Granular Grounding for Document QA","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2026/html/Venna_M3Grounder_Mask-Based_Multi-Span_and_Multi-Granular_Grounding_for_Document_QA_CVPR_2026_paper.html","authors":["Venkata Kesav Venna","Sai Madhusudan Gunda","Jyothi Swaroopa Jinka","Hrithik Sagar Rachakonda","Anirudh Srinivasan","Ravi Kiran Sarvadevabhatla"],"year":2026,"venue":"CVPR 2026","abstract":"Links individual generated answer spans to pixel-level evidence masks in document images. It also represents evidence at nested phrase, line, and block granularities and evaluates multi-span grounding on complex document layouts."}
{"title":"DLaVA: Document Language and Vision Assistant for Answer Localization with Enhanced Interpretability and Trustworthiness","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.00151","arxiv_id":"2412.00151","authors":["Ahmad Mohammadshirazi","Pinaki Prasad Guha Neogi","Ser-Nam Lim","Rajiv Ramnath"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-11-29","abstract":"Adds answer-localization capabilities to multimodal models for Document VQA so answers can be spatially traced back to their source locations rather than evaluated only for textual correctness."}
{"title":"BBox DocVQA: A Large Scale Bounding Box Grounded Dataset for Enhancing Reasoning in Document Visual Question Answer","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15090","arxiv_id":"2511.15090","authors":["Wenhan Yu","Wang Chen","Guanqiang Qi","Weikang Li","Yang Li","Lei Sha","Deguo Xia","Jizhou Huang"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-11-19","abstract":"Introduces a DocVQA dataset with explicit supporting bounding boxes, including single-region, multi-region, single-page, and multi-page questions. The benchmark directly evaluates fine-grained evidence localization together with answer generation."}
{"title":"DocTrace: Towards Traceable Long Document VQA via Hierarchical Evidence Graph Reasoning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.03292","arxiv_id":"2608.03292","authors":["Le Xiang","Zhicheng Guan","Hong Chen","Xiaocong Lin","Zhenghua Lei","Teng Hu","Bolei He","Long Zeng"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-08-04","abstract":"Models long-document VQA as evidence-graph reasoning. The framework performs evidence localization, structured document parsing, and explicit graph construction with node-level provenance so evidence composition across multiple pages can be inspected."}
{"title":"Look as You Think: Unifying Reasoning and Visual Evidence Attribution for Verifiable Document RAG via Reinforcement Learning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.12003","arxiv_id":"2511.12003","authors":["Shuochen Liu","Pengfei Luo","Chao Zhang","Yuhao Chen","Haotian Zhang","Qi Liu","Xin Kou","Tong Xu","Enhong Chen"],"year":2026,"doi":"10.1609/aaai.v40i38.40488","venue":"AAAI 2026","abstract":"Introduces a Chain-of-Evidence representation that attaches reasoning references to document regions using bounding boxes and page indexes. The reinforcement-learning method trains models to generate answers together with progressively attributable visual evidence."}
{"title":"Benchmarking Retrieval-Augmented Multimomal Generation for Document Question Answering","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16470","arxiv_id":"2505.16470","authors":["Kuicai Dong","Yujing Chang","Shijie Huang","Yasheng Wang","Ruiming Tang","Yong Liu"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-05-22","abstract":"Introduces MMDocRAG for long multimodal documents containing text, images, and tables. Its questions include multi-page cross-modal evidence chains and its evaluation explicitly measures multimodal evidence selection and integration."}
{"title":"Evidence Attribution in Visual Document Understanding without Coordinates or Region Labels","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24651","arxiv_id":"2607.24651","authors":["Zhuchenyang Liu","Yao Zhang","Yu Xiao"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-07-27","abstract":"Studies document evidence attribution without requiring models to directly emit coordinates. Models quote supporting text and a multimodal retriever maps those quotations back to page regions, providing an alternative route from answer evidence to precise source location."}
{"title":"Where is this coming from? Making groundedness count in the evaluation of Document VQA models","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.findings-naacl.295/","doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.findings-naacl.295","authors":["Armineh Nourbakhsh","Siddharth Parekh","Pranav Shetty","Zhao Jin","Sameena Shah","Carolyn Rose"],"year":2025,"venue":"Findings of NAACL 2025","abstract":"Proposes Document VQA evaluation metrics that account for both semantic correctness and multimodal placement of an answer in its source document. Human evaluation is used to validate whether the grounded scoring better distinguishes supported from poorly grounded predictions."}
{"title":"Benchmarking Visual LLMs Resilience to Unanswerable Questions on Visually Rich Documents","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.11468","arxiv_id":"2511.11468","authors":["Davide Napolitano","Luca Cagliero","Fabrizio Battiloro"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-11-14","abstract":"Introduces VRD-UQA for plausible but unanswerable questions over multi-page visually rich documents. Corruptions vary entities, document elements, layouts, and pages, allowing abstention failures to be separated from ordinary answer accuracy."}
{"title":"AdaDocVQA: Adaptive Framework for Long Document Visual Question Answering in Low-Resource Settings","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.13606","arxiv_id":"2508.13606","authors":["Haoxuan Li","Wei Song","Aofan Liu","Peiwu Qin"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-08-19","abstract":"Presents an adaptive framework for question answering over long visual documents, combining document segmentation and retrieval with generated reasoning examples and adaptive inference."}
{"title":"MM-Doc-R1: Training Agents for Long Document Visual Question Answering through Multi-turn Reinforcement Learning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13579","arxiv_id":"2604.13579","authors":["Jiahang Lin","Kai Hu","Binghai Wang","Yuhao Zhou","Zhiheng Xi","Honglin Guo","Shichun Liu","Junzhe Wang","Shihan Dou","Enyu Zhou","Hang Yan","Zhenhua Han","Tao Gui","Qi Zhang","Xuanjing Huang"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-04-15","abstract":"Uses a vision-aware multi-turn agent to iteratively find and synthesize information in long documents. It is relevant to cross-page evidence discovery although its main contribution is agent training rather than a complete fine-grained provenance hierarchy."}
{"title":"DocLLM: A layout-aware generative language model for multimodal document understanding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.00908","arxiv_id":"2401.00908","authors":["Dongsheng Wang","Natraj Raman","Mathieu Sibue","Zhiqiang Ma","Petr Babkin","Simerjot Kaur","Yulong Pei","Armineh Nourbakhsh","Xiaomo Liu"],"year":2024,"abstract":"Represents enterprise-document text together with bounding-box layout information and models cross-alignment between semantic and spatial modalities. It targets irregular layouts and heterogeneous business documents such as forms, invoices, reports, and contracts."}
{"title":"LayoutLLM: Large Language Model Instruction Tuning for Visually Rich Document Understanding","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.892/","authors":["Masato Fujitake"],"year":2024,"venue":"LREC-COLING 2024","abstract":"Integrates text, image, and document-layout information with an instruction-tuned language model for visually rich document understanding tasks."}
{"title":"ERNIE-Layout: Layout Knowledge Enhanced Pre-training for Visually-rich Document Understanding","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2022.findings-emnlp.274/","authors":["Qiming Peng","Yinxu Pan","Wenjin Wang","Bin Luo","Zhenyu Zhang","Zhengjie Huang","Yuhui Cao","Weichong Yin","Yongfeng Chen","Yin Zhang","Shikun Feng","Yu Sun","Hao Tian","Hua Wu","Haifeng Wang"],"year":2022,"venue":"Findings of EMNLP 2022","abstract":"Uses layout-centered pretraining, including explicit reading-order prediction, to learn representations combining document text, layout, and image information."}
{"title":"VRDU: A Benchmark for Visually-rich Document Understanding","url":"https://research.google/pubs/vrdu-a-benchmark-for-visually-rich-document-understanding/","authors":["Zilong Wang","Yichao Zhou","Wei Wei","Chen-Yu Lee","Sandeep Tata"],"year":2023,"venue":"KDD 2023","abstract":"Benchmarks information extraction from visually rich business documents with diverse layouts, nested fields, tables, multi-column structure, and template variation representative of industrial document workflows."}
{"title":"Semantic Table Structure Identification in Spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3460319.3464812","doi":"10.1145/3460319.3464812","authors":["Yakun Zhang","Xiao Lv","Haoyu Dong","Wensheng Dou","Shi Han","Dongmei Zhang","Jun Wei","Dan Ye"],"year":2021,"venue":"ISSTA 2021","abstract":"Defines semantic spreadsheet-table structure through header types and relations, including hierarchy, aggregation, units or value names, spatial organization, merged cells, formatting cues, and formula-derived relationships."}
{"title":"SpreadsheetBench: Towards Challenging Real World Spreadsheet Manipulation","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.14991","arxiv_id":"2406.14991","authors":["Zeyao Ma","Bohan Zhang","Jing Zhang","Jifan Yu","Xiaokang Zhang","Xiaohan Zhang","Sijia Luo","Xi Wang","Jie Tang"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-06-21","abstract":"Introduces a benchmark built from real spreadsheet-user requests and heterogeneous spreadsheet files containing multiple tables, non-standard structures, and non-textual elements. It evaluates end-to-end spreadsheet manipulation rather than normalized-table QA alone."}
{"title":"SpreadsheetBench 2: Evaluating Agents on End-to-End Business Spreadsheet Workflows","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.29955","arxiv_id":"2606.29955","year":2026,"published":"2026-06-29","abstract":"Evaluates agents on professional spreadsheet generation, debugging, and visualization workflows involving complex workbooks. Tasks average many worksheets and require coordinated modifications and cross-sheet dependencies rather than isolated table operations."}
{"title":"Towards Robust Real-World Spreadsheet Understanding with Multi-Agent Multi-Format Reasoning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.12282","arxiv_id":"2604.12282","authors":["Houxing Ren","Mingjie Zhan","Zimu Lu","Ke Wang","Yunqiao Yang","Haotian Hou","Hongsheng Li"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-04-14","abstract":"Presents SpreadsheetAgent, which incrementally inspects spreadsheet regions through code results, rendered images, and LaTeX tables. It first constructs structural sketches and row or column summaries and then verifies relevant regions during downstream reasoning."}
{"title":"Back to the Future: A workbook time machine for spread sheet creation benchmarks","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.07873","arxiv_id":"2608.07873","authors":["Mansi Uniyal","Agamdeep Singh","Ananya Singha","Priyanshu Gupta","Mukul Singh","Gust Verbruggen","Vu Le","Sumit Gulwani"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-08-08","abstract":"Introduces a pipeline that creates spreadsheet benchmarks from before-and-after workbook states. The resulting tasks cover formulas, charts, pivot tables, and conditional formatting and therefore preserve richer workbook structure than plain-table benchmarks."}
{"title":"General Table Question Answering via Answer-Formula Joint Generation","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.12345","arxiv_id":"2503.12345","authors":["Zhongyuan Wang","Richong Zhang","Zhijie Nie"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-03-16","abstract":"Treats spreadsheet formulas as logical forms for complex table question answering and jointly generates an answer and its formula. It provides evidence about formula-based reasoning but does not by itself establish full workbook-level understanding."}
{"title":"TRH2TQA: Table Recognition with Hierarchical Relationships to Table Question-Answering on Business Table Images","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/WACV2025/html/Jirachanchaisiri_TRH2TQA_Table_Recognition_with_Hierarchical_Relationships_to_Table_Question-Answering_on_WACV_2025_paper.html","authors":["Pongsakorn Jirachanchaisiri","Nam Tuan Ly","Atsuhiro Takasu"],"year":2025,"venue":"WACV 2025","abstract":"Extracts business-table images into structured representations that preserve merged cells and parent-child header relationships before performing table QA. The work directly targets hierarchical table structure needed to interpret complex financial documents."}
{"title":"Split, Embed and Merge: An accurate table structure recognizer","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.05214","arxiv_id":"2107.05214","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2022.108565","authors":["Zhenrong Zhang","Jianshu Zhang","Jun Du","Fengren Wang"],"year":2022,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Recognizes table structure by splitting images into a fine grid, combining visual and textual features for grid elements, and merging grids into cells. The method explicitly handles complex tables and spanning cells and outputs cell coordinates, spans, and content."}
{"title":"Robust Table Detection and Structure Recognition from Heterogeneous Document Images","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patcog.2022.109006","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2022.109006","authors":["Chixiang Ma","Weihong Lin","Lei Sun","Qiang Huo"],"year":2023,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Combines table detection with split-and-merge structure recognition to reconstruct cell grids and spanning cells from heterogeneous document images, including tables with blank areas, distortions, and complex geometry."}
{"title":"Table Structure Recognition Based on Grid Shape Graph","url":"https://doi.org/10.23919/APSIPAASC55919.2022.9980172","doi":"10.23919/APSIPAASC55919.2022.9980172","year":2022,"venue":"APSIPA ASC 2022","abstract":"Represents table structure through a grid-shape graph designed to retain global rows and columns while also recognizing spanning cells. The approach predicts grid localization and grouping relationships to recover logical cell structure."}
{"title":"Transformer-based dynamic cell bounding box refinement for end-to-end Table Structure Recognition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patrec.2025.11.011","doi":"10.1016/j.patrec.2025.11.011","authors":["Yang Xue","Haosheng Cai","Zhuoming Li","Lianwen Jin"],"year":2026,"venue":"Pattern Recognition Letters","abstract":"Adds a coordinate decoder that iteratively refines individual cell bounding boxes while jointly modeling table structure. The method is particularly relevant when cell-level provenance must survive table extraction."}
{"title":"Scene-Text Oriented Referring Expression Comprehension","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TMM.2022.3219642","doi":"10.1109/TMM.2022.3219642","authors":["Yuqi Bu","Liuwu Li","Jiayuan Xie","Qiong Liu","Yi Cai","Qingbao Huang","Qing Li"],"year":2022,"venue":"IEEE Transactions on Multimedia","abstract":"Defines a referring-expression task in which linguistic descriptions can refer to text visible inside an image. Its model explicitly aligns scene-text semantics, visual regions, and referring expressions, making it a close transfer analogue for references such as labels or highlighted content in screenshots."}
{"title":"Bridging the Gap between Expression and Scene Text for Referring Expression Comprehension (Student Abstract)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v36i11.21597","doi":"10.1609/aaai.v36i11.21597","authors":["Yuqi Bu","Jiayuan Xie","Liuwu Li","Qiong Liu","Yi Cai"],"year":2022,"published":"2022-06-28","venue":"AAAI 2022","abstract":"Grounds referred image objects while explicitly using scene text as an identifying cue. Extracted text is assigned to corresponding visual regions and matched against the referring expression."}
{"title":"Knowledge Mining of Scene Text for Referring Expression Comprehension","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-70549-6_15","doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-70549-6_15","authors":["Chenyang Gao","Biao Yang","Wenwen Yu","Yuliang Liu","Xiang Bai"],"year":2024,"venue":"ICDAR 2024","abstract":"Extends scene-text-aware referring-expression comprehension by exploiting scene-text information when grounding natural-language expressions to visual regions."}
{"title":"Unambiguous Scene Text Segmentation With Referring Expression Comprehension","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TIP.2019.2930176","doi":"10.1109/TIP.2019.2930176","authors":["Xuejian Rong","Chucai Yi","Yingli Tian"],"year":2019,"venue":"IEEE Transactions on Image Processing","abstract":"Introduces language-conditioned segmentation of specific scene-text instances. Referring expressions are mapped to pixel-level text regions, providing transfer evidence for grounding language to precise text-rich image regions."}
{"title":"A model for multimodal reference resolution","url":"https://aclanthology.org/J00-2002/","doi":"10.1162/089120100561665","authors":["Luis Pineda","Gabriela Garza"],"year":2000,"venue":"Computational Linguistics","abstract":"Provides an early formal model for resolving natural-language names and pronouns against graphical objects in a multimodal message, explicitly treating the antecedent as potentially residing in a graphical rather than linguistic context."}
{"title":"GRAVL-BERT: Graphical Visual-Linguistic Representations for Multimodal Coreference Resolution","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2022.coling-1.22/","authors":["Danfeng Guo","Arpit Gupta","Sanchit Agarwal","Jiun-Yu Kao","Shuyang Gao","Arijit Biswas","Chien-Wei Lin","Tagyoung Chung","Mohit Bansal"],"year":2022,"venue":"COLING 2022","abstract":"Resolves cross-modal coreferences in multi-turn dialogue by jointly modeling scene objects, visual relationships, dialogue history, and metadata. It is transfer evidence for resolving message expressions against attached visual content."}
{"title":"Disambiguating Reference in Visually Grounded Dialogues through Joint Modeling of Textual and Multimodal Semantic Structures","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.547/","doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.acl-long.547","authors":["Shun Inadumi","Nobuhiro Ueda","Koichiro Yoshino"],"year":2025,"venue":"ACL 2025","abstract":"Unifies textual reference resolution and grounding to visual objects in dialogue, with particular attention to ambiguous pronouns and ellipses. This is transfer evidence for references in communication text that point into an associated visual artifact."}
{"title":"Not All References Resolve Alike: Fine-Grained Assessment of Complementary Cross-modal Reference Resolution","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/411853600_Not_All_References_Resolve_Alike_Fine-Grained_Assessment_of_Complementary_Cross-modal_Reference_Resolution","authors":["Eleftherios Kapernaros","Katerina Pastra"],"year":2026,"venue":"SETN 2026","abstract":"Studies cross-modal reference resolution at a fine-grained level, examining how meanings expressed in one modality are associated with entities or events expressed in another. It is transfer evidence rather than a workplace-document benchmark."}
{"title":"Semi-supervised multimodal coreference resolution in image narrations","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.emnlp-main.682/","doi":"10.18653/v1/2023.emnlp-main.682","authors":["Arushi Goel","Basura Fernando","Frank Keller","Hakan Bilen"],"year":2023,"venue":"EMNLP 2023","abstract":"Studies coreference resolution and fine-grained narrative grounding when a longer text is paired with an image. The setting is a transfer analogue for resolving expressions in a message against associated visual evidence."}
{"title":"A machine-learning approach for analyzing document layout structures with two reading orders","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patcog.2008.03.014","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2008.03.014","authors":["Chung-Chih Wu","Chien-Hsing Chou","Fu Chang"],"year":2008,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Uses learned split-or-merge decisions to identify text lines and regions in documents that may contain both horizontal and vertical reading orders. It establishes reading order as a structural property distinct from OCR text accuracy."}
{"title":"The document spectrum for page layout analysis","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/34.244677","doi":"10.1109/34.244677","authors":["Lawrence O'Gorman"],"year":1993,"venue":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","abstract":"Introduces the docstrum, a bottom-up nearest-neighbor method for structural page-layout analysis that estimates text-line and block organization while remaining robust to skew, variable spacing, and multiple local orientations."}
{"title":"Recursive X-Y cut using bounding boxes of connected components","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDAR.1995.602059","doi":"10.1109/ICDAR.1995.602059","authors":["Jaekyu Ha","Robert M. Haralick","Ihsin T. Phillips"],"year":1995,"venue":"ICDAR 1995","abstract":"Presents an efficient recursive X-Y page-segmentation algorithm operating on connected-component bounding boxes. The resulting hierarchical rectangular decomposition is foundational for preserving region-level document structure."}
{"title":"A prototype document image analysis system for technical journals","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/2.144436","doi":"10.1109/2.144436","authors":["George Nagy","Sharad C. Seth","Mahesh Viswanathan"],"year":1992,"venue":"Computer","abstract":"Describes a document-image analysis and parsing system for technical journals. Its X-Y tree representation converts two-dimensional page segmentation into a hierarchical structure suitable for subsequent logical parsing."}
{"title":"Page segmentation and classification","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/1049-9652(92)90068-9","doi":"10.1016/1049-9652(92)90068-9","year":1992,"venue":"CVGIP: Graphical Models and Image Processing","abstract":"Segments scanned pages into structural blocks and classifies regions such as text, graphics, and halftones. It is foundational evidence that document understanding requires typed spatial regions rather than a flat OCR stream."}
{"title":"A fast algorithm for bottom-up document layout analysis","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/34.584106","doi":"10.1109/34.584106","authors":["Anikó Simon","J.-C. Pret","A. Peter Johnson"],"year":1997,"venue":"IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence","abstract":"Presents a bottom-up document-layout algorithm for organizing page components into higher-level structural regions, extending early work on geometric page decomposition."}
{"title":"Document Analysis System","year":1982,"abstract":"An early document-image analysis system that separates text regions from other page content and addresses recognition across varied printed-document layouts. It is foundational evidence for physical and logical document-structure analysis predating modern Document AI."}
